  "notes": "The country-pop duet ballad specialists — tenor-and-high-tenor harmony over piano/synth beds. The entry names one thing \"the structural signature\" and this model is built around it: \"several singles are drumless for the whole first verse, then enter with a programmed clap-and-sub before the live kit arrives at chorus 2 — three-stage dynamic staging,\" with \"16th shaker throughout; big gated snare on the final chorus.\" That is the sparsest kick in this batch, a clap layer, a continuous shaker and the widest accent-to-main velocity spread. The 808 is authored in `counter_riff` because the entry places both layers and gives the sub a stage rather than the whole record: \"synth sub under a simple electric bass; the sub is often the only low end in verse 1.\" Harmony carries a specific voicing claim — \"IV–I/3–V pop voicings and suspended chords delaying resolution\" — which is the high `susSubstitutionProb`; the slash-bass inversion is not encodable as a numeral and is left to the voicing. Melody is \"the highest male tessitura in this section — chorus lines sit in the upper tenor with sustained belted peaks, plus real melisma and falsetto tags,\" so the register ceiling is the highest of any male model here. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF] and the entry notes one single reads ~51 or ~102 at the double. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the 808 register, the velocity spread and the counter ratio.",
